  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Zimbabwe Agriculture Development Trust</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to strengthen the lending capacity of at least four (4) commercial banks and six (6) microfinance institutions to provide financial services to youth and women-led start-up and growth-oriented agribusinesses. 

The project will contribute to the Sida funded, three-year Creating Adaptive Unique Systems for financing Entrepreneurial Youth and Women (CAUSEWAY) Project implemented by the Zimbabwe Agriculture Development Trust (ZADT). The main objective is to improve access to finance for youth and women in peri-urban and rural areas of Zimbabwe who are running sustainable and growth-oriented enterprises that improve and increase their household incomes and food security.</narrative>
  </description>
